  "raw_meta_yaml": "context:\n  version: \"0.2.2\"\n\npackage:\n  name: twobitreader-rs\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://pypi.org/packages/source/t/twobitreader-rs/twobitreader_rs-${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 2be192ab7fad3a0a72e0cdb304151e2af45f13cfc8d2c0ad350e7dd218b9d817\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  skip:\n    - match(python, \"<3.9\")\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    # The Rust toolchain links libgcc_s for unwinding; the C compiler's run-export is what\n    # puts libgcc into `run` and satisfies conda-build's overlinking check.\n    - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n    - ${{ compiler('rust') }}\n    - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n    - cargo-bundle-licenses\n    - if: build_platform != target_platform\n      then:\n        - python\n        - cross-python_${{ target_platform }}\n        - maturin >=1.15,<2.0\n  host:\n    - python\n    - pip\n    - maturin >=1.15,<2.0\n  run:\n    - python\n\ntests:\n  - python:\n      imports:\n        - twobitreader_rs\n      pip_check: true\n  - script:\n      - python -c \"from twobitreader_rs import reverse_complement; assert reverse_complement('ACGTN') == 'NACGT'\"\n      - python -c \"from twobitreader_rs import TwobitReader; assert hasattr(TwobitReader, 'get')\"\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://github.com/andrewdelong/twobitreader-rust\n  summary: Fast DNA sequence extraction from 2bit files\n  description: |\n    Python bindings for the twobitreader Rust crate. Reads the UCSC 2bit genome format\n    through a memory map, with batched extraction, exon concatenation, reverse complement,\n    and prefetching for files not yet in the page cache.\n  license: MIT OR Apache-2.0\n  license_file:\n    - LICENSE-MIT\n    - LICENSE-APACHE\n    - THIRDPARTY.yml\n  documentation: https://docs.rs/twobitreader\n  repository: https://github.com/andrewdelong/twobitreader-rust\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - andrewdelong\n",
